right team\n- Spot follow-ups that may need attention\n- Start the day with a shared view of support priorities\n\nChoose the Slack channel that makes the most sense for your team—whether that’s a dedicated support channel, a customer-success workspace, or a team-wide updates channel.\n\n## Get started\n\nConnect Slack from your helpdesk settings, select the channel where you’d like summaries posted, and you’re ready to go.\n\nThe integration is available now for existing customers. Set it up today and make support visibility part of your team’s daily workflow.\n=== END OF TEXT A ===\n\n=== TEXT B ===\n## New: Daily Open Ticket Summaries in Slack\n\nKeeping your support team aligned just got easier.\n\nYou can now connect your helpdesk to Slack and receive a daily summary of open support tickets in the channel of your choice. Give your team a clear view of outstanding work—without needing to log in and check dashboards first thing in the morning.\n\nEach daily summary helps your team quickly understand what needs attention, including the current volume of open tickets and the tickets that may require follow-up.\n\n### Why it matters\n\nWith daily ticket visibility in Slack, your team can:\n\n- Start the day with a shared view of open support work  \n- Keep support, customer success, and account teams in sync  \n- Spot growing backlogs before they become urgent  \n- Discuss priorities and coordinate next steps where your team already works  \n\nWhether you send the summary to a dedicated support channel or a cross-functional team channel, everyone who needs visibility can stay informed.\n\n### Get started\n\nSet up the Slack integration from your helpdesk settings, choose the Slack channel where you’d like summaries delivered, and enable daily notifications.\n\nOnce connected, your team will receive a reliable daily snapshot of open tickets—right in Slack.\n\nConnect Slack today and make sure no open customer conversation gets overlooked.\n=== END OF TEXT B ===\n\nAn